WEBVTT

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.140
If you want to adopt an animal,

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.520
first we need to know some references.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:14.620
References?

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:16.740
People we know?

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.320
Friends, teachers....

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.200
We need to talk to some people about you.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.340
We want to be sure that you're responsible

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.800
and that you can take good care of an animal.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.400
Then you have to fill out this form

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.520
about your family background.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:32.840
Is that it?

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.560
No, there's more.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:38.740
We need to know about your history with animals.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.400
Have you ever owned an animal?

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:41.100
Yes.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.200
We had a cat when I was eight years old.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.460
I love cats.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.420
Do you have any animals now?

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.380
Unfortunately, no.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.260
Anything else?

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.020
We also like to know

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.600
your reasons for wanting an animal.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:57.180
Just to hold it and cuddle with it.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.040
Just to have as a pet.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.340
I love animals.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.600
To have a friend -- a pal.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.760
You know, man's best friend is his dog.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.380
And one thing more.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.480
If you're under twenty-one years of age ...

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.080
That's me.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.020
Then an adult must sign for you.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:15.740
Uh-oh.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:17.480
No problem.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.560
My parents will think it's a good idea.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.180
I'll be back with them.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.120
If the real owners don't come to claim Gemma ...

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.280
After forty-eight hours.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:27.600
But please call first.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.020
Thanks for your information and for being so helpful.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.220
It's my pleasure.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.980
Nice talking to both of you.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:35.920
Thanks again.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:36.440
Bye.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.000
Maybe the real owners will come to claim her.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.120
Her eyes look so sad.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:44.700
She must really miss them.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.460
I see you're both animal lovers.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:47.540
We are.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.720
We'll call in a couple of days.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.340
Bye.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.620
I keep thinking about the dog -- about Gemma,

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:08.940
alone in the animal shelter.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:10.560
I know.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.200
the dog is just fine.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.100
They're very kind to the animals.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.820
I know they are.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.380
I mean about her being alone.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.080
Even if they are kind to Gemma,

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.980
she's still alone, without her family.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:25.480
Ready, folks?

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.280
Are you ready, Alexandra?

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:28.440
Yes, I'm ready.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.180
I'll have the chef's salad, please.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.280
I will have a cheeseburger, medium rare,

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.300
with raw onion, and french fries, please.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:39.400
Anything to drink?

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:40.920
A diet cola, please.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.080
Ginger ale with lots of ice for me, thank you.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.000
I've got it.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:45.520
Thanks.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:48.300
Aren't you surprised

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.300
that the animal shelter is so careful

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.220
about finding homes for the animals?

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:53.380
No, I'm not.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.060
And a cheeseburger, medium rare,

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.480
with onion and french fries.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.880
And a ginger ale with lots of ice.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:02.280
Salad dressing?

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:06.460
Hey, I wanted you to hear my new sound system

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.280
when the dog scratched on the front door.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:09.920
Let's finish eating,

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.200
and then we'll go back to my house.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.960
I want you to hear my new tapes.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.080
I've got some great new dance music.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:38.460
Hello.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.620
Is Robbie Stewart there?

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:40.650
This is he.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:41.220
Who's this?

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.780
This is Linda Aborn from the animal shelter.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.220
It's Linda from the animal shelter.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.290
Yes, Linda.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:48.600
Hi.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:51.740
Oh?

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.680
The good news is that the Levinsons have come by

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:55.560
to pick up the dog.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.020
The bad news is, you won't be able to adopt the dog.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.200
Come by one day and look at some of the other dogs.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:05.960
I'm sure there's one for you.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:07.080
Thanks, Robbie.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.020
And the Levinsons thank you for bringing their dog to us.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:11.620
Thanks, Linda.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:12.740
Bye.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:24.180
That's right.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.200
I'm glad for the dog.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.580
I guess I am, too.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.880
She said if I come by,

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:32.360
she'll help me find another dog.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:35.970
Come on.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:36.500
Let's dance.
